 ## Background
-Sequential CSG is a sequential CPU implementation of voxel grid Boolean operations operating on `HostVoxelsGrid` structures [S1, unofficial]. It provides a CPU-based alternative to GPU-accelerated voxel boolean operations, serving as a foundational component in the CSG Model Voxelization pipeline [2497-csg-model-voxelization.md]. The method leverages word-level parallelism to improve efficiency over per-voxel operations while maintaining the simplicity of a sequential algorithm [S1, unofficial].
